From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 11:06:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-microsoft-surface-duo: one board DT
 (no test layers, no overlay)

The board DTS includes exactly the twelve Duo dtsi files the default DTB was made of (it used to be layered: board DTS + appended dtsi + build-test-dtb extras + an fdtoverlay for the flash LED + fdtput patches). The flash LED is a normal dtsi now; unused experiments (camss-noiommu, imx351-bob, ipa, l17a-3v0, venus-axicrst) are removed. make dtbs reproduces the running default DTB (tools/linux/dts/dtb-compare.py: identical apart from phandle numbering).

This patch was written by Claude (Anthropic's AI assistant) under the direction of Bryson, who reviewed and
tested it on a Surface Duo.

Signed-off-by: Bryson <10244083+brysonwf@users.noreply.github.com>
---
